Full transcripts: the events of task tskB5TWUin4RqY in byre (GET /api/events?task_id=tskB5TWUin4RqY).

## Summary

Performance audit of heliosian at 948bf93. Production share cards for events, parties, and activities were redrawn on every request (the busiest card, 176 times in a week, median 0.53s). The server now keeps each finished PNG in a 32MB process cache keyed by the card's etag, and the When, Celebrate, and HCA-Team handlers answer from that cache before reading the picture from storage.

A card whose picture failed to load is still returned for that request and is not stored, so a later successful read draws the picture. Whole versus cropped is part of those three keys, so a flyer and a photo of the same upload do not share a card. The app name and subtitle are read once per draw and reused for the painting, the key, and the response.

The cache was chosen over a faster scaler: bilinear scaling changes pixels, and faster PNG compression saved about 15ms while making a larger file. A local repeat dropped from about 47ms to about 34µs. There is no singleflight; two misses at once may both draw. The etag does not include the picture bytes, so a hit skips storage. A client that saved the etag of a picture-less card can still get 304 for it.

Left alone: When search still embeds on every keystroke (now a Helios When item in TODO.md; it is rare, and debouncing would change when results appear), directory person cards still rebuild per keystroke, and wiki share cards still read markdown before drawing. The cache is per process, so the first request and a new instance still draw.

Main had moved picture loading into cardPicture and the calendar lines into whenCardLines. The merge keeps those helpers and the cache behavior.

